WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.166 --> 00:00:02.102
This just in to CNN.

00:00:02.102 --> 00:00:05.105
Tucker Carlson is out at Fox News.

00:00:05.105 --> 00:00:09.442
The right wing network just announced
the two have parted ways.

00:00:09.876 --> 00:00:13.613
CNN senior media reporter
Oliver Darcy is here with more on this.

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:16.649
What are you learning?
He was out on Friday.

00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:19.486
Will we see him say goodbye?
We're not going to see him say goodbye.

00:00:19.519 --> 00:00:21.921
This is really stunning news
coming from Fox.

00:00:21.955 --> 00:00:24.124
They say his last show was April 20.

00:00:24.124 --> 00:00:26.326
First they put out a very short statement.

00:00:26.326 --> 00:00:28.028
They said they think him for his service.

00:00:28.028 --> 00:00:29.863
And that's that's all we know. Right now.

00:00:29.863 --> 00:00:32.699
But of course, this comes days
after last week, you remember.

00:00:32.932 --> 00:00:36.569
Fox News
settled this massive defamation lawsuit

00:00:36.569 --> 00:00:39.706
with Dominion voting systems over
the election lies that it promoted

00:00:39.706 --> 00:00:44.044
in the wake of the 2020 election
so they paid out $787 million

00:00:44.177 --> 00:00:48.214
the highest known defamation settlement
ever publicly known in U.S.

00:00:48.214 --> 00:00:48.515
media.

00:00:48.515 --> 00:00:49.883
So this is coming days after that.

00:00:49.883 --> 00:00:51.818
Unclear,
of course whether this is related.

00:00:51.818 --> 00:00:55.055
It's kind of hard to imagine that
these coincidentally these things happen.

00:00:55.055 --> 00:00:58.892
Tucker Carlson was sowing doubts
about the US election results

00:00:59.459 --> 00:01:01.127
Just up until the last few weeks.

00:01:01.127 --> 00:01:04.064
So it's possible
that there was a relationship there.

00:01:04.064 --> 00:01:07.934
But really big news and I should also
point out that they've stuck with them

00:01:08.168 --> 00:01:09.702
really through quite a lot.

00:01:09.702 --> 00:01:12.872
Like he has promoted
conspiracy theories about the vaccines.

00:01:12.872 --> 00:01:16.242
He has said things
that are just blatantly anti-immigrant.

00:01:16.443 --> 00:01:20.680
He has, like I said, promoted
that doubt about the 20, 20 election.

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:22.949
They have stuck with him
throughout all of this.

00:01:23.183 --> 00:01:27.187
So, you know, really shocking news
that now he's no longer with the network.

00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:29.456
Yeah. The big question as you say, is why?

00:01:29.789 --> 00:01:31.958
Why now?

00:01:31.958 --> 00:01:34.694
Fox has let their number
one people go before.

00:01:34.694 --> 00:01:37.864
I mean, Bill O'Reilly,
they pushed out when he was number one

00:01:37.997 --> 00:01:40.133
they're doing this now
with Tucker Carlson.

00:01:40.300 --> 00:01:43.636
We talk about this happening
in the wake of the Dominion decision.

00:01:44.571 --> 00:01:46.739
Now, it's interesting with Carlson,

00:01:46.739 --> 00:01:49.476
which is that it wasn't his show

00:01:49.976 --> 00:01:54.514
or he shows that Dominion was suing over
necessarily for promoting false news.

00:01:54.514 --> 00:01:57.550
It was some of his behind the scenes stuff
that was legally problematic.

00:01:57.784 --> 00:02:00.887
For Fox,
but he wasn't one of the people who helped

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:02.789
get them in trouble with Dominion, was he?

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:06.059
No, he wasn't the main culprit
that really spawned this lawsuit.

00:02:06.059 --> 00:02:10.196
But, you know, it's not to say also
that other hosts could not be eventually

00:02:10.196 --> 00:02:11.364
leaving the network as well.

00:02:11.364 --> 00:02:14.734
I mean, this raises a lot of questions
about whether the network potentially

00:02:14.734 --> 00:02:19.873
is trying to at least rein in some of
the more extreme people on the channel.

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:23.643
I mean, of course, Tucker Carlson,
the most extreme probably on that channel.

00:02:23.977 --> 00:02:26.446
I should also note, John,
why this is so important.

00:02:26.579 --> 00:02:27.814
I mean, Tucker Carlson outside.

00:02:27.814 --> 00:02:32.752
Donald Trump really was the person
commanding the GOP really directing it.

00:02:32.752 --> 00:02:37.023
You saw Republican lawmakers, prominent
Republican lawmakers often grovel

00:02:37.023 --> 00:02:37.690
at his feet.

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:41.461
Ted Cruz, Ted Cruz, for instance, grovel,
that is he and others because they were

00:02:41.461 --> 00:02:46.566
afraid of of him going on his primetime
show and lashing out at them.

00:02:46.566 --> 00:02:47.700
So this is not

00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:51.437
only huge news in the world of media,
but also in the world of politics

00:02:51.437 --> 00:02:55.775
where he was really pushing
the GOP in that extremist direction.

00:02:56.009 --> 00:02:57.911
In this.
Also, just to that point,

00:02:57.911 --> 00:03:01.447
this all also his show is also a place
that a lot of Republican lawmakers

00:03:01.848 --> 00:03:05.251
or anyone who wanted to speak to Donald
Trump would go

00:03:05.451 --> 00:03:07.453
in order to send their message
because they knew

00:03:07.453 --> 00:03:10.223
that Donald Trump would be watching
and so closely tracking

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:13.560
that show in and of itself, doing it
where he was in his contract.

00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:16.563
Are they going to be able to say
that this was and of his contract?

00:03:16.563 --> 00:03:17.864
They just want to try something different?

00:03:17.864 --> 00:03:20.500
I'm I'm not sure.
I mean, I have been reaching out.

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:23.069
I have also reached out to Tucker Carlson
and and everyone

00:03:23.436 --> 00:03:26.372
trying to get more information on this
but this is a very short statement.

00:03:26.372 --> 00:03:28.875
Also, notably,
there's no statement from Tucker Carlson.

00:03:28.875 --> 00:03:29.943
And here, you know,

00:03:29.943 --> 00:03:33.446
it doesn't seem if I have to guess,
that they parted ways amicably.

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:37.083
We'll be obviously looking
for more information in the hours ahead.

00:03:37.183 --> 00:03:40.887
I think the other question here is
it's not just about this defamation case

00:03:40.887 --> 00:03:42.188
that has already been settled.

00:03:42.188 --> 00:03:43.356
There is more to come.

00:03:43.356 --> 00:03:46.092
There's more legal action
Smartmatic and others.

00:03:46.092 --> 00:03:49.229
And it does make you wonder
if this has something to do with that,

00:03:49.229 --> 00:03:52.765
because it is so abrupt and
it doesn't seem amicable at this point.

00:03:52.765 --> 00:03:53.733
Not with that. Right.

00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:56.569
There's a lot more legal action
on the way for Fox News.

00:03:56.569 --> 00:04:00.974
They have the Smartmatic lawsuit,
which is a $2.7 billion lawsuit that's

00:04:00.974 --> 00:04:04.544
also making its way through the courts
and that hasn't been resolved yet.

00:04:05.078 --> 00:04:08.448
So it's potentially possible
that, you know, Fox News just had enough.

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:12.218
They maybe have needed a scapegoat,
someone to just kind of throw and say,

00:04:12.218 --> 00:04:13.453
look, we got rid of this guy.

00:04:13.453 --> 00:04:13.720
I mean,

00:04:13.720 --> 00:04:16.923
because they do have some other problems
with with shareholders probably upset

00:04:17.190 --> 00:04:21.761
that they had these election deniers
go on air and knowingly spread falsehoods.

00:04:21.761 --> 00:04:25.665
So, you know, there's a lot of things
at play, but there is so much, you know,

00:04:26.332 --> 00:04:29.168
that was happening for so long
before we got to this point, right?

00:04:29.369 --> 00:04:31.704
Yeah.
But now they've had to pay $787 million

00:04:31.704 --> 00:04:35.208
and they have shareholders
who are not happy about that.

00:04:35.241 --> 00:04:36.442
I mean, that's a lot of money.

00:04:36.442 --> 00:04:37.076
We'll see.

00:04:37.076 --> 00:04:41.114
Look, it's hard to imagine Fox
all of a sudden just changing the way

00:04:41.214 --> 00:04:42.782
it does business completely.

00:04:42.782 --> 00:04:44.250
They've had to do payouts before.

00:04:44.250 --> 00:04:46.853
Let me read this statement
because it is so short. Yeah.

00:04:47.153 --> 00:04:50.823
It says Fox News Media and Tucker
Carlson have agreed to part ways.

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:54.294
We thank him for his service
to the network as a host and prior to that

00:04:54.294 --> 00:04:55.261
as a contributor.

00:04:55.261 --> 00:04:58.998
Mr. Carlson's
last program was Friday, April 21st.

00:04:59.165 --> 00:05:01.801
That's really incredible. In its brevity.

00:05:01.801 --> 00:05:07.206
There As for Tucker Carlson,
this may sound outlandish to some,

00:05:07.507 --> 00:05:11.277
but there are people who suggested that
maybe he would become

00:05:11.277 --> 00:05:15.148
a Republican candidate himself,
and that's because of the firm grip

00:05:15.148 --> 00:05:17.984
he has exerted over
the GOP in the last few years.

00:05:18.217 --> 00:05:18.985
I mean, he

00:05:18.985 --> 00:05:24.223
I should say this is the top rated host,
not only on Fox, but really all of cable.

00:05:24.257 --> 00:05:28.528
I mean, he was commanding a huge audience,
a huge audience,

00:05:28.528 --> 00:05:30.496
and he was very influential over
that audience.

00:05:30.496 --> 00:05:32.131
It was a very loyal audience.

00:05:32.131 --> 00:05:32.765
They tuned in.

00:05:32.765 --> 00:05:34.133
If you look at the ratings,

00:05:34.133 --> 00:05:38.204
the ratings would spike on Fox News
specifically for Tucker Carlson.

00:05:38.204 --> 00:05:41.741
And so, yes, he has a huge sway over
GOP primary voters.

00:05:41.741 --> 00:05:44.010
I think that's why those questions
were raised.

00:05:44.177 --> 00:05:46.679
Whether he would
potentially run for president one day,

00:05:47.413 --> 00:05:50.350
you know, doesn't seem like that's
probably why he's leaving,

00:05:50.350 --> 00:05:52.485
given the statement in the way
this just ended here.

00:05:52.552 --> 00:05:56.823
But, you know, one,
we we've decided to part ways is not a way

00:05:56.823 --> 00:05:59.492
you send off your top rated,

00:06:00.059 --> 00:06:03.262
top rated anybody on
any show for any reason.

00:06:03.463 --> 00:06:07.266
You don't cast them aside or part ways
with them unless something is wrong.

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:10.403
I mean, he was on the list
for four possible witnesses

00:06:10.536 --> 00:06:13.172
when it came for the truth to the Dominion
Voting Trust.

00:06:13.172 --> 00:06:15.408
He was supposed to be
one of the one of the first witnesses

00:06:15.641 --> 00:06:16.776
that they called to the stand.

00:06:16.776 --> 00:06:20.012
And of course, that got averted
when they when they had that settlement.

00:06:20.046 --> 00:06:23.583
But we should also point out, too,
he is so extreme.

00:06:23.583 --> 00:06:25.952
I mean, the things that he was doing on
this program

00:06:25.952 --> 00:06:27.754
make Sean Hannity look like a moderate.

00:06:27.754 --> 00:06:32.458
I mean, it started off more as he was
a mainstream conservative figure,

00:06:32.458 --> 00:06:36.896
but he has really been radicalized
in recent years and he's also radicalized

00:06:36.896 --> 00:06:37.530
his audience.

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:41.000
I mean, the things that were promoted on
his show used to be what you would see

00:06:41.000 --> 00:06:45.938
on Infowars, which is that far right
company hosted and founded by Alex Jones.

00:06:45.938 --> 00:06:49.976
He was also facing over
$1,000,000,000 in legal problems.

00:06:50.176 --> 00:06:53.179
But it was being mainstream to the Fox

00:06:53.179 --> 00:06:56.349
News audience,
which is obviously very dangerous.

00:06:56.349 --> 00:07:00.620
And so it's potentially possible
that Fox thinks it can get away

00:07:00.620 --> 00:07:01.187
with so much

00:07:01.187 --> 00:07:02.088
more like Sean Hannity,

00:07:02.088 --> 00:07:05.725
who promotes a lot of conspiracy theories
himself, but is a little bit

00:07:05.725 --> 00:07:09.729
more mainstream, not as radical as Tucker
has been letting this go on for years.

00:07:09.729 --> 00:07:11.697
This is not like New York.

00:07:11.697 --> 00:07:13.366
So it's interesting,
the timing of all this.

00:07:13.366 --> 00:07:14.700
We'll have to wait and see what he says.

00:07:14.700 --> 00:07:17.503
I'm sure there will be something
coming out from his side of things.

00:07:17.537 --> 00:07:19.872
Well, that's actually one
that's kind of an interesting question.

00:07:19.872 --> 00:07:22.308
Though, because what we do know
when it comes to Fox

00:07:22.308 --> 00:07:25.344
and when they part ways
with someone there, just ask

00:07:25.344 --> 00:07:28.614
Gretchen Carlson
and the nondisclosure agreement.

00:07:28.614 --> 00:07:29.982
And also the interesting thing, too, is,

00:07:29.982 --> 00:07:33.753
is he free to jump to another network
if that's what something he wants to do?

00:07:34.353 --> 00:07:38.191
Newsmax, if he jump to Newsmax,
which is that smaller right wing channel

00:07:38.191 --> 00:07:42.462
that Fox News was really worried
about in the wake of the 2020 election,

00:07:43.062 --> 00:07:45.431
his audience,
I'm sure, would follow him over there.

00:07:45.465 --> 00:07:47.767
So is he free to do that?
Is that something he wants to do?

00:07:47.967 --> 00:07:50.102
Is it possible
he wants to do something like Glenn Beck

00:07:50.102 --> 00:07:52.171
started his own media empire on the side?

00:07:52.171 --> 00:07:55.241
There's a lot of different options for him
here, depending on what his contract is.

00:07:55.241 --> 00:07:57.477
And I will say the legal problems
for Fox throughout over

00:07:57.477 --> 00:07:58.878
they have the Smartmatic lawsuit

00:07:58.878 --> 00:08:02.815
Smartmatic has sued Fox
for more than Dominion did.

00:08:02.949 --> 00:08:06.385
And now you have a potential disgruntled

00:08:06.752 --> 00:08:09.422
employee, Tucker Carlson,
as a witness there.

00:08:09.422 --> 00:08:14.360
And we should say this to last week
after this Dominion lawsuit was settled,

00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:17.897
you saw Tucker Carlson
kind of poke the eye of everyone

00:08:17.897 --> 00:08:21.267
when he went on this program
and was just talking about,

00:08:21.267 --> 00:08:24.504
can you imagine a media company
openly lying to the viewers?

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:28.474
It seemed like a subtle reference
to what Fox News was accused of

00:08:28.474 --> 00:08:30.610
and him trying to make it
about the rest of the media.

00:08:30.610 --> 00:08:34.247
So, you know,
he really was someone who didn't

00:08:34.247 --> 00:08:36.182
seem bound
by the normal rules over at Fox.

00:08:36.182 --> 00:08:38.484
And now his time
there is coming to an end.

00:08:38.484 --> 00:08:40.620
All right, Oliver Darcy, keep us posted.

00:08:40.653 --> 00:08:42.321
I imagine there will be more coming out.

